      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Marengo County Historical Society sits in the 1870 Laird Cottage, which also houses the Geneva Mercer Museum honoring a native sculptor who worked with Giuseppe Moretti.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/demopolis/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Demopolis lies at the confluence of the Black Warrior and Tombigbee rivers, forming a navigable waterway that once powered the city’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
